<title>SINGAPORE: Khong Guan half year profits down sharply.</title>
<headline>Khong Guan half year profits down sharply.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended October 31 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     0.04    vs     0.45</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		  0.40    vs     4.99</p>
<p>    Turnover				54.42    vs    43.69</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest	 0.44    vs     0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation    0.06    vs     0.06</p>
<p>    Associates			    (0.07)   vs     0.56</p>
<p>    Taxation				 0.18    vs     0.30</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.22    vs     0.11</p>
<p>    Extraordinary			 (0.20)   vs     2.40</p>
<p>Note - Kong Guan Flour Milling Ltd said the group's profit for the first half was affected by the adverse result incurred by  its principle operating subsidiary in raw commodities trading. In addition, its associated company Far East Biscuit Factory (HK) Ltd, suffered a small half year loss due to seasonal trade factors and austere measures imposed to control the rate of economic growth in its principle market. It did not expect group profit for the full year to be maintained at the previous year's level.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
